WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 line:92%
-I want to ask about this,

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.369
because one of the things
that happened this week --

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
we all remember
famously July 27, 2016,

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:10.143
Donald Trump said if, "Russia,
if you're out there listening,

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd love to see
Hillary Clinton's e-mails,"

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
basically invited them
to hack her server.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.717
And it came up this week that
Robert Mueller basically said,

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
that day, they tried.
-Yes.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:23.890 size:81% position:41%
-So you confronted him
at the rally that day

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
about his comments.
-Yeah.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was it
that he said to you?

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was the -- By the way,
it was the weirdest --

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:31.164
one of the weirdest moments in
what was a very weird campaign.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's very --
Be careful with the --

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:33.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know. I know.
-Yeah.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.068 size:81% position:41%
There were a lot of --
Now I'm thinking back,

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there were a lot.
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah, right.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.371
-But this one was particularly
weird -- particularly weird.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were in the middle
of one of his golf courses.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're in a ballroom,
this very gaudy ballroom

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
with this patterned carpet.
-He has a -- All right.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I'm just gonna say it.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- It was a little
over -- over-decorated. Fine.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was also really freezing
in there.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like he was trying
to freeze us

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:57.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
or send us to Siberia.
-[ Laughing ] Okay, got you.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:57.657 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And he comes out.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.692
It's the middle of the
Democratic National Convention.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.829
Usually, presidents or
presidential candidates go dark

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they're not having
their convention,

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.266 line:92%
but he wants the attention,

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there had been some rumors
about hacking --

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.670 size:88% position:44%
the DNC had been hacked,
some e-mails came out,

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was very embarrassing
for the DNC,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was talk
about maybe it being Russia.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.242 line:92%
Nothing had been confirmed yet.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was all
kind of bubbling out there.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.112 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Donald Trump comes out

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
and starts talking
about Russia all of a sudden

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how everybody thinks that
Russia is hacking.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:23.883 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"They're not hacking.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, oh, by the way,
I want to see those e-mails."

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:31.157
And I remember sitting there
and thinking, "Uh, wait. What?

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did Donald Trump just ask
a foreign government

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.929
to hack
into Hillary Clinton's e-mails?

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:36.629 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Did that just happen?"

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's even weird
by Donald Trump's standards.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.701
-Sure.
-And -- And I remember thinking,

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I got to ask this guy
about it,"

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
and at this time,
he kind of hates me,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he's not letting me
ask questions.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the next couple questions
that came out

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
were about something else,
about the economy

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:54.714
or something just totally
not on the topic of Russia.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.851
And I remember thinking, "Well,
maybe I'm the crazy person.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe that's
a totally normal thing,

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's just part
of politics, and I'm naive.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
But eventually, I decide that,
no, it's a big question,

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've got to get
his attention.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm waving my arm
frantically,

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.563 line:92%
and he's not calling on me.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I go back
to my tried and true strategy,

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:13.967 size:84% position:42% line:92%
which is to flatter him

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
in order to get him
to pay attention to me.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:18.872
And so I said, "Your poll
numbers are really great!"

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he turns and looks at me,
and he says, "Katy!"

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:25.278 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Katy, is that you?

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.149 line:92%
Are you wearing a disguise?

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:29.816 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Oh, no, that is you."

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said "Yes,
your poll numbers are great.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.453 line:92%
Let me ask you about Russia.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.854 line:92%
Does it not give you pause

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.957
to ask a foreign government
to hack into the election?"

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
He doesn't even let me finish
the sentence.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.995 line:92%
"No, it does not give me pause.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:42.962 line:92%
What should give you pause

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
is Hillary Clinton
and her missing e-mails."

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"Hold on. Hold on. Hold on."

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.103
You are asking
a foreign government to meddle."

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.939
And he's like, "You're
just trying to save her."

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:53.873 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And I said, "No, no.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.242 size:84% position:42%
You're asking a foreign
government to meddle."

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he keeps steamrolling
over me,

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.245 line:92%
and he, at the end of it, says,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:02.048 size:88% position:44%
"No, I would really like
to see those e-mails."

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.349 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So that was a huge day.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is an American
presidential candidate

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
asking for help
from a foreign government,

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.222 size:88% position:44% line:92%
doing it very blatantly.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.523 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was very weird.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:12.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then,
the campaign continues on,

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:16.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he says a whole bunch
of other totally crazy things.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:16.496 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the intelligence
community...

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-Yeah, we just have to like --

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.401
Then we just throw stuff away.
We don't have room in there.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:24.204
-Everything gets -- gets totally
buried by the next controversy,

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.573
which is what actually ended up
really helping him,

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:29.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you couldn't focus
on just one thing.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:29.809 line:92%
And a lot of folks asked,

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.145 size:78% position:39%
"Well, why didn't you
press that harder?"

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.447 line:92%
We had no indication whatsoever

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
from anybody
in the intelligence community.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:39.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
Peter Strzok wasn't texting
any of us and saying,

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, I got this information
on Donald Trump."

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.156 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We had no idea.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.691 line:92%
The only hint we had to it

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:48.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
was that press release
that came out on October 7th,

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.463 size:81% position:41%
which was also the day
that Donald Trump --

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:53.967
well, the tape came out
where Donald Trump was bragging

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
about grabbing women
by certain parts.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. No memory.
No memory of that.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:59.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-So that got buried.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:03:59.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That got buried.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:00.907 line:92%
And it was only a press release

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:01.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
that said
Russia wanted to meddle.

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:05.678
It had nothing to do with --
with Donald Trump's campaign.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.980 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Fast-forward to today,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, oh, my God,
that date is so significant.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.318
We had it come out in the --
in the indictment that Russia --

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.154
that Mueller put out on Friday,
saying July 27th,

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:18.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
the day Donald Trump said,
"Russia, if you're listening,"

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:21.027
that is the day that the
conspirators in the indictment,

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:24.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
these 12 Russians,
started for the first time --

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it says
it in the indictment --

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:28.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the first time --
tried to get into

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hillary Clinton's e-mails
and server.

